        <section id="faqs" class="py-3">
            <h2 class="pipe">Frequently Asked Questions About Services in Bolton, MA</h2>
            
            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates handle subsurface ledge rock during excavation in Bolton, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates utilizes heavy hydraulic excavators equipped with rock hammers and mechanical rippers to break apart shallow subsurface ledge rock common in Worcester County. Excavated rock material is systematically removed or crushed on-site for structural fill, followed by the installation of dense-graded processed gravel. This site preparation method provides a stable, level foundation for subsequent asphalt paving, foundation footings, or retaining wall construction in Bolton.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What is the recommended asphalt pavement specification for steep driveways in Bolton, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates installs a 2-inch binder course of dense binder HMA followed by a 1.5-inch top course of fine-aggregate bituminous concrete for steep Bolton driveways. Subgrade preparation includes heavy geotextile fabric and a 6-to-8 inch compacted gravel base to prevent washouts. Extruded asphalt Cape Cod berms are installed along driveway edges to direct heavy stormwater runoff away from residential structures and prevent shoulder erosion.</p>
